        itemId = 44719,
        name = "Frenzyheart Brew",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Unlock Frenzyheart Revered and repeat ripened jars until the toy appears.\n\n1. If the Sholazar factions are not unlocked, kill Pitch near 50.5, 76.5 and accept Playing Along from Tracker Gekgek. Follow High-Shaman Rakjak's jobs at Frenzyheart Hill (55.0, 69.2) through Just Following Orders, help the injured Oracle, then follow the Rainspeaker Canopy story through A Hero's Burden. The initial jobs for both sides are part of the unlock.\n\n2. Enter Artruis's cave at 70.9, 58.7 and reach him around 72.2, 57.5. Let his encounter release Jaloot and Zepik. Kill JALOOT, keep ZEPIK alive, then defeat Artruis to choose Frenzyheart. Avoid area damage and instant kills that skip the choice; remove damage gear and control your attacks if overlevelled.\n\n3. Speak to surviving Zepik inside the cave. Complete Frenzyheart Champion and take Return of the Lich Hunter back to Frenzyheart Hill. If switching from the Oracles, finish these normal follow-ups before expecting the hill's dailies; merely killing Artruis does not complete the change.\n\n4. At Frenzyheart Hill, complete the available daily quests and return for the next daily reset until Revered. Keep the quest's supplied companion available when its objectives require it. Remaining with Frenzyheart while buying jars avoids switching back and losing access to their quartermaster.\n\n5. Buy a Disgusting Jar (44717) from Tanak at 55.0, 69.0. Keep it for THREE real-time days until it becomes a Ripe Disgusting Jar (44718). This timer continues while logged out; the old seven-day duration is obsolete.\n\n6. Open the ripe jar. If it contains Frenzyheart Brew, use the Brew to add the toy. Otherwise buy another jar and repeat the three-day cycle. The jar is Unique, so you cannot queue several fermenting jars on one character.",
        sourceType = "Reputation",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=44719",
